**Answer:** J) 130.28 … 498.88 °F  

**Explanation**

The heat‑transfer problem is a cylindrical series‑resistance case.  
For a pipe of inner radius \(r_i\), outer radius \(r_o\) and a surrounding insulation whose outer radius is \(r_{ins}\),

\[
\dot Q = \frac{2\pi L\,(T_i-T_o)}
               {\displaystyle\frac{\ln(r_o/r_i)}{k_{\text{steel}}}
                +\frac{\ln(r_{ins}/r_o)}{k_{\text{ins}}}}
\]

where  

* \(T_i=500\ ^\circ\text{F}\) (inner steel surface)  
* \(T_o=150\ ^\circ\text{F}\) (outer insulation surface)  
* \(L=1\) ft (heat loss per foot of pipe)  

**Geometry (in feet)**  

\[
\begin{aligned}
r_i &= \frac{6\ \text{in}}{2}=3\ \text{in}=0.25\ \text{ft}\\[2pt]
r_o &= \frac{6.5\ \text{in}}{2}=3.25\ \text{in}=0.2708\ \text{ft}\\[2pt]
r_{ins} &= r_o + 3.5\ \text{in}=3.25\ \text{in}+3.5\ \text{in}
         =6.75\ \text{in}=0.5625\ \text{ft}
\end{aligned}
\]

**Thermal resistances**

\[
\begin{aligned}
R_{\text{steel}} &= \frac{\ln(r_o/r_i)}{2\pi k_{\text{steel}}}
                  =\frac{\ln(0.2708/0.25)}{2\pi(26)}
                  =2.55\times10^{-4}\ \frac{^\circ\!F\cdot\text{ft}}{\text{heat}}\\[4pt]
R_{\text{ins}}   &= \frac{\ln(r_{ins}/r_o)}{2\pi k_{\text{ins}}}
                  =\frac{\ln(0.5625/0.2708)}{2\pi(0.04)}
                  =1.17\times10^{-1}\ \frac{^\circ\!F\cdot\text{ft}}{\text{heat}}
\end{aligned}
\]

Total resistance  

\[
R_{\text{tot}} = R_{\text{steel}}+R_{\text{ins}}
               \approx 0.1175\ \frac{^\circ\!F\cdot\text{ft}}{\text{heat}}
\]

**Heat loss per foot**

\[
\dot Q = \frac{T_i-T_o}{R_{\text{tot}}}
       = \frac{500-150}{0.1175}
       \approx 130.3\ \frac{\text{heat}}{\text{hr·ft}}
\]

which matches the numerical value in choice J.

**Interface temperature**

The temperature drop across the steel wall is  

\[
\Delta T_{\text{steel}} = \dot Q \, R_{\text{steel}}
                       = 130.28 \times 2.55\times10^{-4}
                       \approx 0.033\ ^\circ\!F
\]

Hence the temperature at the pipe–insulation interface is  

\[
T_{\text{int}} = T_i - \Delta T_{\text{steel}}
               \approx 500 - 0.033
               \approx 498.9\ ^\circ\!F
\]

Rounded to two decimals, this is **498.88 °F**, again the value listed in choice J.  

Thus the correct pair is **130.28 … 498.88 °F** (choice J).<|return|>
